third-party

--- code ---

test/uu.l, the ported section only (from "UniMath Foundations PartA")
  Copyright (c) 2015 the UniMath Development Team.
  MIT License. https://github.com/UniMath/UniMath
  Definitions and theorem statements from Foundations/PartA.v et al, ported to
  uu's surface with the original names.

src/love/audio/opus/, the Opus codec (decoder; the encoder half is removed)
  Copyright 1994-2011 IETF Trust, Xiph.Org, Skype Limited, Octasic, Jean-Marc Valin,
  Timothy B. Terriberry, CSIRO, Gregory Maxwell, Mark Borgerding, Erik de Castro Lopo.
  BSD 3-Clause; the full text in src/love/audio/opus/COPYING.
  The reference implementation from RFC 6716, its float build, compiled as one unit
  by src/love/audio/opus.c. Each file keeps its own license header.

src/apps/hearts/perlasm.l
  A port of Linux's lib/crypto/arm64/sha2-armv8.pl, by Andy Polyakov for the OpenSSL
  project (CRYPTOGAMS), which he relicensed under the GPLv2 for the kernel, as that
  file's header states. GNU General Public License version 2
  (SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0), not the tree's 0BSD. Its templates are read at
  run time from the pinned upstream copy.

src/apps/hearts/patches/0001-raspberrypi-tryboot.patch
  A patch to Linux's drivers/firmware/raspberrypi.c (Copyright © 2015 Broadcom).
  GNU General Public License version 2, as the kernel it patches
  (SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0), not the tree's 0BSD.


--- data ---

src/apps/tls/roots.pem
  Mozilla's CA certificate program: the roots trusted for serving tls, as extracted
  from NSS's certdata.txt by curl (https://curl.se/docs/caextract.html), verbatim.
  Mozilla Public License 2.0. https://www.mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/

src/apps/kore/fs.l, the `udc-db` string
  GNU coreutils' dircolors database, verbatim, as `dircolors -p` prints it.
  Copyright (C) 1996-2026 Free Software Foundation, Inc.
  Copying and distribution of this file, with or without modification, are
  permitted provided the copyright notice and this notice are preserved. The
  notice is kept inline.

src/apps/moon/lib/moonlibc/ctype/ucdctype.h, ucdwidth.h, ucdemoji.h
  Generated by src/tools/mkctype.l, mkwidth.l and mkemoji.l from the Unicode
  Character Database 17.0.0 (https://www.unicode.org/Public/17.0.0/ucd/).
  © 2025 Unicode®, Inc.
  Unicode License v3. https://www.unicode.org/license.txt

src/apps/vi/config.l, the `hue-theme` values but Identifier's and Special's
  From molokai (https://github.com/tomasr/molokai), Copyright (c) 2011 Tomas Restrepo,
  based on the Monokai theme for TextMate by Wimer Hazenberg and its darker variant
  by Hamish Stuart Macpherson. MIT License.


--- fonts ---

src/love/quay/cga_8x8.c
  Public domain. Letters, digits and Latin-1 from font8x8 by Daniel Hepper
  (https://github.com/dhepper/font8x8), after Marcel Sondaar's copy of IBM's
  public domain VGA fonts; pictures, box lines, blocks and maths from unscii-8
  by viznut (http://viznut.fi/unscii/). Four glyphs drawn for the tree.

src/love/quay/cleat_8x16.c
  Terminus Font, Copyright (c) 2020 Dimitar Toshkov Zhekov,
  with Reserved Font Name "Terminus Font".
  SIL Open Font License 1.1. https://terminus-font.sourceforge.net/
  The cp437 console face (ter-i16n.psf) re-laid on quay's page order by
  src/tools/mkpsf.l. A modified version may not wear the reserved name, so the
  table is named for the tree.


--- music ---

src/apps/lore/grass.l, the `score` list
  "Toy Soldiers", written by Martika and Michael Jay, 1988.
  The tune the music box plays is an arrangement by ear of its chorus melody.

src/apps/lore/grass99.l, the `score99` list
  "I Want It That Way", written by Max Martin and Andreas Carlsson, recorded by the
  Backstreet Boys, 1999.
  The tune the music box plays is an arrangement of the title line.
